        this.val = val;
        this.next = null;
    }
}
*/

class Solution {
    searchKey(head, key) {
        if (head === null) {
            return false;
        }

        if (head.val === key) {
            return true;
        }

        return this.searchKey(head.next, key);
    }
}
```

Time complexity: `O(n)` when the key is absent or appears at the end.

Space complexity: `O(n)` for the recursion stack in the worst case.

Recursion makes the two cases clear: an empty pointer means the search failed, while a matching value means the search succeeded. Otherwise, the same check continues from the next node.

For example, with `7 -> 3 -> 9` and key `9`, the calls check `7`, then `3`, then `9`, and the last call returns `true`.

