🔹 Approach

To search a key in a singly linked list, we use linear traversal.

👉 Start from the head
👉 Move node by node (next)
👉 Compare each node’s value with key
👉 If found → return true
👉 If end reached (null) → return false
//-------------------------------------------

Linked List does not support indexing like arrays, so we must check each node sequentially.

//-------------------------------------------

🔹 Algorithm Steps
    Initialize a pointer current = head
    while current !== null
    If current.val === key → return true
    Move current = current.next
    If loop ends → return false

